<Layout
  title="Airbnb Price Optimizer | Jacob A. Torres"
  description="Predicting Airbnb listing prices with linear regression, XGBoost, and a Keras neural network."
>
  <a href="/projects#data-science" class="back-link">&larr; Back to Projects</a>

  <article class="article-body">
    <div class="article-header">
      <h1>Airbnb Price Optimizer</h1>
      <p class="article-subtitle">
        Entering the 21st-century travel market with math and Python
      </p>
      <p class="article-date">
        <time datetime="2020-12-20">December 20, 2020</time>
      </p>
    </div>

    <p>
      When traveling around the United States, an increasing number of people
      are looking to the popular service
      <a
        href="https://airbnb.com/"
        rel="external noopener">Airbnb</a
      > as an alternative to more traditional options like hotels. There are several
      main reasons for this trend, including the flexibility of location, housing
      type, and affordability. It's important for a person interested in listing
      their home for rent on Airbnb to understand what determines a fair price, so
      they can enter this booming market with full confidence.
    </p>

    <p>
      The dataset was found on
      <a
        href="https://kaggle.com/datasets/"
        rel="external noopener">Kaggle's database</a
      > and comprises nearly a quarter of a million Airbnb listings around the United
      States in 2020. Thanks to
      <a
        href="https://github.com/singparvi"
        rel="external noopener">Parvi Singh</a
      > for collaboration on modeling and deployment.
    </p>

    <p>
      The code for this project lives in the
      <a
        href="https://github.com/jacob-torres/AirBnB-Optimal-Price"
        rel="external noopener"
        >Airbnb Optimal Price repository</a
      >.
    </p>

    <h2>Tools</h2>

    <ul>
      <li>pandas, NumPy, and Matplotlib</li>
      <li>
        scikit-learn: LinearRegression, One-Hot encoder, OrdinalEncoder,
        SimpleImputer, StandardScaler
      </li>
      <li>XGBoost: XGBoost Regressor</li>
      <li>TensorFlow: Keras Sequential model</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Exploratory data analysis</h2>

